# Documentation

- Short, decision-oriented docs: **why** a choice was made, not a restatement of the code.
- Update README for setup, scripts, test, build, and deploy when those exist.
- Record non-obvious architecture (data layer, i18n, auth) in README or `docs/` only when it helps onboarding.
- Do not duplicate Cursor rules in long-form docs; link or rely on `.cursor/rules/` for agent standards.
- ADRs optional—use for irreversible or controversial choices only.
